{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgSzPZV3oofTcUBVjAU2M", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I would fix the `findByEmail` bug in `src/services/auth-service.js:5` first. It is the only one with a direct access-control impact. The predicate ignores `deleted_at`, so `isActive` in the same file returns true for a soft-deleted account. Any code that gates login or access on `isActive` would let deleted users through. The other two bugs produce wrong totals in reporting-style functions, which is a correctness problem but does not grant access to anything. They are still worth fixing, but after this one.\n\nI have not changed any files."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1977, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16819, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 1977, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": "toolu_01XFSpYDjcagtcKetjAtcgGX", "agent_id": "a8ecbecde8f05baf8", "session_id": "9dfac4f3-7136-4ed2-86ed-902f94671817", "uuid": "267c4a26-be12-41df-970e-15e081a4db63", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T15:37:24.394Z", "request_id": "req_011CgSzPZBCoTUZzRmBSwEwK", "subagent_type": "test-runner", "task_description": "Run test suite"}
